			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Replace legacy TauriIPCServer documentation with atomic placeholder\n\nRemove the verbose legacy documentation from `Source/IPC/TauriIPCServer/mod.rs` which detailed the batched, single-file synchronization model. Replace the content with a concise module header indicating this is now the placeholder for the new atomic Tauri IPC server orchestrator.\n\nThe old implementation is preserved in the sibling path `IPC::TauriIPCServer_Old` for reference. This change aligns the `Source/IPC` directory with the project's shift towards fine-grained state management and clears the namespace for the upcoming rewrite of the communication bridge between Mountain and Wind. An `allow(non_snake_case)` attribute is added to suppress lints during the transition period as consumers migrate to the new `Server::TauriIPCServer` entry point.",
